295 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 157 0 R
/E (In this course students will become actively engaged in meaningful and authentic uses of the Spanish language. They will develop a variety of skills that will allow them to use Spanish in a myriad of authentic situations. Specifically, students will use the following modes of communication: Interpretive Mode = Comprehend reading and listening materials in Spanish, Interpersonal Mode = Engage in conversations with speakers of Spanish, Presentational Mode = Present information and ideas in both written and spoken formats of Spanish.  In addition, cultural information is woven throughout this course in order to expose students to the people, geographical locations, food, music and other cultural aspects of the Spanish-speaking world. \(**Locally-developed Proficiency Examination as the final exam in June\). \(NCAA-Approved\))
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
