397 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 162 0 R
/E (The Dual Language Program is systematic in nature. The effects of education are cumulative and the full benefits are only evident over the long term of the enriched educational experience. It is important for families to commit to the program throughout the school year. Active parent involvement in the program is required to sign a commitment agreement. Families are essential partners in our Dual Language Immersion program. Research shows that long-term family involvement is critical to program success. When parents engage consistently and value bilingualism, children are more likely to thrive academically, socially, and culturally. This is a long-term journey, and the full benefits of bilingualism and biliteracy become evident over time. \(Cloud, Genesee & Hamayan, 2000; Arlington Public Schools, 2023\) Hence, parents of students in the program will be required to sign a commitment agreement and commit to the program.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
